        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/517608?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC extends the set of Unicode character which can be used in identifiers with <a href=\"https://util.unicode.org/UnicodeJsps/list-unicodeset.jsp?a=%5B%3AID_Compat_Math_Start%3DYes%3A%5D&amp;g=&amp;i=idtype\" rel=\"nofollow\">ID_Compat_Math_Start</a> and <a href=\"https://util.unicode.org/UnicodeJsps/list-unicodeset.jsp?a=%5B%3AID_Compat_Math_Continue%3DYes%3A%5D&amp;g=&amp;i=idtype\" rel=\"nofollow\">ID_Compat_Math_Continue</a>, most notable: ∇, ∂, ∞, subscripts ⁰¹²³⁴⁵⁶⁷⁸⁹⁺⁻⁼⁽⁾ and superscripts ₀₁₂₃₄₅₆₇₈₉₊₋₌₍₎.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This can be a boon to implementers of scientific concepts as they can write for example <code class=\"notranslate\">let ∇E₁₂ = 0.5;</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Danvil/rfcs/blob/compat_math_identifiers/text/3840-compat-math-identifiers.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3840",
            "title": "RFC: ID_Compat_Math characters allowed in identifiers",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-02T22:01:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-16T19:17:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Danvil",
                "url": "https://github.com/Danvil"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1295100?u=b0540abe14ddfb8c24578add2a8c960bc704a661&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Supercedes <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1241693645\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3268\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3268/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3268\">#3268</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Extends Rust's existing SIMD infrastructure, <code class=\"notranslate\">#[repr(simd)]</code>, with a complementary scalable representation, <code class=\"notranslate\">#[repr(scalable)]</code>, to support scalable vector types, such as Arm's Scalable Vector Extension (SVE), or RISC-V's Vector Extension (RVV).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Like the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(simd)</code> representation, <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(scalable)</code> is <strong>internal compiler infrastructure that will be used only in the standard library</strong> to introduce scalable vector types which can then be stablised. Only the infrastructure to define these types are introduced in this RFC, not the types or intrinsics that use it.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>It is hoped that the majority of the interesting properties of these types from the perspective of the language team are proposed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2662434146\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3729\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729\">#3729</a>.\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Any further restrictions that this RFC proposes are those that are strictly necessary due to limitations of the codegen backend.</li>\n<li>It is not expected that this RFC would be accepted in the short-term, only after <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2662434146\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3729\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729\">#3729</a> and its dependencies are accepted.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>This RFC isn't a significant departure from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1241693645\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3268\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3268/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3268\">#3268</a>, but it is being re-opened as much of the discussion on it is no longer relevant - there were many iterations and changes in scope since being opened in 2022.</li>\n<li>Given that this proposes a perma-unstable attribute for use in the standard library and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2662434146\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3729\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3729\">#3729</a> defines the majority of the interesting properties of these types, I hope that this RFC can be under the purview of t-compiler/t-libs - I've asked about this in <a href=\"https://rust-lang.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/213817-t-lang/topic/question.3A.20responsible.20team.20for.20repr.28scalable.29\" rel=\"nofollow\">#t-lang on Zulip</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/davidtwco/rfcs/blob/repr-scalable/text/3838-repr-scalable.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3838",
